WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.850
Hollywood has an embarrassingly poor track
record when it comes to adapting anime properties

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.609
for the silver screen.

00:00:06.609 --> 00:00:10.769
And if the negative reaction to Ghost in the
Shell is anything to go by, that's not likely

00:00:10.769 --> 00:00:12.480
to change anytime soon.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.500
Hollywood hasn't abandoned their attempts
to find the right approach to anime remakes,

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.000
but some of the stuff is just too weird for
western sensibilities.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.699
Prison School

00:00:22.699 --> 00:00:26.300
On the surface, Prison School seems like the
kind of property that might fit right in with

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.210
other dystopian teen flicks.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:32.800
But the way this anime shows its young characters
struggling against injustice is nothing like

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:33.980
The Hunger Games.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:38.620
This adaptation of Akira Hiramoto's manga
series follows five boys who get accepted

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:43.120
into a prestigious school that was formerly
only available to female students.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.890
After almost immediately getting caught peeping
in the girl's locker room, the boys are thrown

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:49.280
in the school's own horrific prison.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:53.760
What happens is way too graphic to describe
here, but it's safe to say that Hollywood

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.710
isn't likely to consider buying the rights
to a show that blends high school life with

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:01.250
Fifty Shades of Grey anytime soon.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:03.100
No Game No Life

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:08.280
The overwhelming popularity of Sword Art Online
has not only been responsible for a boom in

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:13.470
MMORPG-themed anime, but also paved the way
for advances in real life virtual reality

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:14.470
gaming.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:17.640
But while a live-action series of Sword Art
is currently being developed for U.S. television,

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:22.790
that isn't likely to happen with another series
called No Game No Life.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:27.350
This anime is the story of Sora and his little
sister Shiro, two reclusive gamers who are

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:32.020
transported to a world called Disboard by
the God of Gaming after they defeat him in

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:33.190
a game of chess.

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:37.710
Once there, the siblings launch a plan to
usurp the reigning god and take over.

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:42.700
The story in itself is pretty standard in
the emerging MMORPG genre, though the extremely

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:48.490
creepy relationship between Sora and his 11-year-old
little sister raises numerous red flags.

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:52.010
That's all we can really say about that, but
it's pretty safe to assume that you'll never

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:54.451
see No Game No Life on the big screen in the
US.

00:01:54.451 --> 00:01:59.450
And you may be put on a list even if you watch
the anime.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:00.950
Sekkou Boys

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:06.409
Recently named among the best idol anime of
all time by My Anime List, Sekkou Boys is

00:02:06.409 --> 00:02:08.700
also one of the most bizarre, idol or otherwise.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:14.150
The show follows the exploits of Miki, a recent
graduate who lands a dream job managing an

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.450
all new idol group, which isn't that unusual….

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:21.090
except this idol group is made up of four
Greco-Roman busts.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.200
Yeah.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:27.900
Singing stone busts Saint Giorgio, Medici,
Hermes, and Mars take the idol world by storm

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:32.280
with Miki's help, which mainly involves wheeling
them from gig to gig in a wheelbarrow.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:36.930
The offbeat humor and crazy set up that made
this unique show so popular would undoubtedly

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:40.550
be lost in the transition to the big screen.

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:42.080
Elfen Lied

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:47.019
Originally airing in 2004, Elfen Lied came
to the attention of western audiences after

00:02:47.019 --> 00:02:49.200
the success of Stranger Things.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.620
Just like the Duffer Brothers hit, Elfen Lied
follows a girl with mysterious powers as she

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:58.159
escapes experimentation at a government facility
and wreaks havoc on her captors.

00:02:58.159 --> 00:03:02.200
The sibling creators of Stranger Things were
quick to acknowledge the show as an influence

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.989
once people started noting the similarities.

00:03:04.989 --> 00:03:08.769
Even still, there's too much violence for
Lucy's story to make it to the screen intact,

00:03:08.769 --> 00:03:13.040
and there's one terrible instance of animal
abuse that would be enough to give Hollywood

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.550
execs nightmares.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:18.840
It makes the subsequent brutal murder of her
tormentors satisfying to watch, but animal

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.319
lovers beware.

00:03:21.319 --> 00:03:22.550
Kinnikuman

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:27.019
First conceived by the writer and artist team
known as "Boiled Egg", Kinnikuman initially

00:03:27.019 --> 00:03:32.600
started out as a parody of '60s sci-fi series
Ultraman, but was also largely influenced

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:35.650
by the rise in popularity of pro-wrestling
in Japan.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:40.000
The story follows the missing prince of planet
Kinniku as he attempts to prove himself worthy

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.510
of his title through wrestling competitions
with other Super Men, all of whom are embodiments

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:46.880
of the places they represent.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:50.591
Even though branded action figures flooded
American toy stores back in the '80s, one

00:03:50.591 --> 00:03:54.790
of the reasons the anime never really made
it to the US because of the character Brockenman,

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:58.450
a full-fledged Nazi who would wrestle in an
SS-themed outfit.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:03.700
The fact that they attempted to make his son
Brocken Jr. a "good Nazi" was even worse in

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.110
many ways.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:10.200
Despite its cult status in Japan, Kinnikuman
is way off the Hollywood radar.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.989
Mysterious Girlfriend X

00:04:11.989 --> 00:04:17.400
Equal parts engrossing and just plain gross,
Mysterious Girlfriend X is the unconventional

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:24.060
love story of 16 year old Akira and his loner
classmate Mikoto, two teens who bond over…

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.110
spit.

00:04:26.169 --> 00:04:29.920
Realistic or not, Hollywood execs aren't about
to get excited over a love affair based on

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:33.500
a saliva fetish, no matter how well received
it's been in Japan.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.080
Plus, you'd be hard pressed to find a pair
of actors willing to spit in each other's

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.080
mouths.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:42.180
That hasn't stopped anime fans from wanting
to see more animated weirdness, however.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:46.820
Only a single season exists right now, despite
plenty of unused material from the original

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:47.820
manga.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:52.220
A petition was started to bring Mysterious
Girlfriend X back, though studio Hoods Entertainment

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.760
has yet to oblige.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.550
Akikan!

00:04:56.550 --> 00:05:01.340
Translating to English as 'Empty Can', the
utterly bizarre Akikan takes place in a world

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:05.390
where anthropomorphic soda cans do battle
to determine which type of drink container

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:07.680
is superior: steel or aluminum.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:13.250
Caught up in this perplexing soda war is high
school student Kakeru, a collector of rare

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:18.330
soda containers who is taken by surprise when
his can of melon soda transforms into a beautiful

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.389
human girl.

00:05:19.389 --> 00:05:24.270
The creatively-named Melon needs to be regularly
infused with carbon dioxide in order to survive

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:28.300
as a human and defeat her competitors, and
Kakeru is more than willing to help.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:31.870
Not only would it be difficult to give any
real resonance to an ongoing battle between

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:36.870
living soda cans, but Akikan's over-the-top
depiction of certain stereotypes just wouldn't

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:38.260
fly in Hollywood.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:41.169
This one's going to have to be kept in the
can.

00:05:41.169 --> 00:05:42.370
Thanks for watching!

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:45.010
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:47.870
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

